  "reuses": [
    "the stripe average (field `stripe`) through flame_veil_blue's `view`s, six of them on a golden-angle spiral plus the frame's own: per loop a soft veil (density 3, power 2) and fine strands (density 10, power 10), screened: crossing strands filling the frame",
    "two of the seven loops painted literal orange and rose (veil and strands): the smouldering streaks; the rest teal from the map",
    "the tone pass with log_density, at the reference's median and p10"
  ],
  "adds": [],
  "notes": [
    "Added: nothing new to the engine: seven loops' stripe crests (veil and strands), two loops painted literal orange and rose for the smouldering streaks and five teal from the map for the crescents, a faint teal hair on the set, the tone pass",
    "Fitted: three red loops of seven (the frame's own among them) read red-heavy against a reference that is mostly slate and teal; two views' worth is the kept balance.",
    "Lessons: item 032 brought five flame references whose look is fine strands and wisps filling the frame (commons_Waves_Apophysis_Fractal_Flame.jpg, convocation-dragons-25.jpg, cosmic-forces-25.jpg, creeping-frost-25.jpg, deaths-icy-hand-25.jpg), after item 028's flame_veil_* scored 2/5 as a few broad sheets. **The strands are the stripe average, not the smooth count**: sheets cut from the smooth count follow its level lines, which nest round the set as rings (through six views at period 0.25 they drew a tunnel of ellipses), while the stripe average's crests run along the orbit's field lines, across the level lines, as fine as its density asks; raised to power 10 only the crests light, and seven loops (the frame and six views on a golden-angle spiral, turned, scaled 0.8 to 1.9 and shifted up to 0.55 frame widths) cross their strands over the whole frame. Under them the same field at density 3 and power 2 is the soft veil. Far from the set the crests run as near-straight rays (ten views at density 8 read as a fan of straight lines); nearer the set they curl, so the strands curl most on seats with set in the frame, and views narrower than the frame (zoom 0.3 to 0.7, centres within 0.25 frame widths: the `close_views` formulation) curl them everywhere, the nearest the round came to the curled ribbons and swirls of convocation-dragons and deaths-icy-hand. **Wisps need far field, as veils did**: of the forty-seat gallery draw (`style scout --n 40`) seven showed the wisps and the rest were filled by lace (the set's own hair floods it), so the locations are item 028's hand-placed shallow seats (its measurement: far-field share median 0.285 over 40 gallery seats, 0.544 over 40 hand seats) with those seven gallery seats (step 4's exception). A full-size frame of seven loops took about two minutes at six threads, a parabolic (r 1.0) or phoenix seat over four; round one is drawn at --draft."
  ],
